                                            <property name="can-focus">False</property>
                                            <property name="halign">start</property>
                                            <property name="valign">start</property>
                                            <property name="label" translatable="yes">&lt;b&gt;Normally closed (NC) switches are strongly recommended.&lt;/b&gt; An NC switch keeps its circuit closed until the axis reaches it, so a broken wire, a loose plug or a switch left unplugged reads as a tripped limit and stops the machine - you find out about the fault straight away.

A normally open (NO) switch only closes when the axis reaches it. If its wire breaks or it is unplugged, nothing looks wrong, but that limit has quietly stopped working, and the axis can run past the end of its travel.

Choose NO only if your switches cannot be wired as NC. The choice applies to all the limit jacks (1-6). The E-stop button is always normally closed.</property>
                                            <property name="use-markup">True</property>
                                            <property name="wrap">True</property>
                                            <property name="xalign">0</property>
                                            <attributes>
                                              <attribute name="font-desc" value="DejaVu Serif 10"/>
                                            </attributes>
