                                                <property name="halign">start</property>
                                                <property name="valign">start</property>
                                                <property name="label" translatable="yes">The signal tower plugs into the signal tower (GX-12/4) plug - check Connected only when one is plugged in. Green is lit while a program, an MDI command or a spindle is running. Red comes on after a following error or a tripped limit switch, and stays on until the machine is turned back on (F2); the buzzer sounds when red comes on.

&lt;b&gt;Sounds&lt;/b&gt; - each can play on the tower's buzzer, on the Pi's own speaker (an HDMI monitor or a USB speaker), on both, or be turned off:
    * Done / Pause Beeps - 3 short beeps when a program, Sync Move or Cut Thread finishes, and 2 when a program stops at M0 or M1 to wait for you.
    * Fault Siren - a 3-second siren when the red light comes on.</property>
                                                <property name="use-markup">True</property>
                                                <property name="wrap">True</property>
