                                <property name="hexpand">True</property>
                                <property name="label" translatable="yes">Checked at every LinuxCNC startup. The gcode directory must never hold a file starting with "Rosetta" (any case) or named M100-M199 - LinuxCNC searches that folder before Rosetta's own subroutines, and before any future Rosetta M-code, so a matching file would quietly run instead of Rosetta's. Rename the file (the Gcode icon on the panel opens that folder) to clear this.</property>
